 "notes": "The in-house 293(2) K P63 22 refinement is used because the final article and abstract interpret diffuse scattering as evidence for partial cation ordering and present P63 22 as the structural model. The same deposited CIF also contains a P-31m refinement, and the article reports that Hamilton tests on merged and unmerged intensities give contradictory symmetry preferences; this ambiguity is preserved rather than hidden. Al, Si, and Fe were constrained to the EPMA fractions on each partially occupied cation site. Hydrogen was determined analytically but was not located by X-ray refinement and is therefore absent from atom_sites. The structural cell volume 83.703(6) A^3 and Z=1 are explicit in the deposited CIF. The executable EOS reference volumes are fitted values for this same conventional cell. This composition is distinct from the existing Mg-rich phase_d material.",
